From f2ccfe12c2d2c9ef4a511b18237381ab44716763 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wim Taymans <wtaymans@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 11:25:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pw-cli: return errno-style error codes from command handlers

So that callers have more information to report useful error
messages.

Backport adaptation: the downstream bind_global() still returns bool, so the
bind_global() callers keep the `!bind_global(...)` form and return -EINVAL on
failure rather than propagating the upstream errno. The security-relevant NULL
checks on pw_core_create_object() in do_create_device/do_create_node and on
pw_registry_bind() path in create_link_with_properties are preserved, and all
pw-cli command handlers are converted to return int to match the
`int (*func)` command-table signature.

